[04/17/25]
Adding this file randomly, bc I forgot to make one when I started this repo LMFAO!!

Levitate is my idea for a truly unique text editor, stemming from a single thought: "What if I could click anywhere on the screen, and start typing?".

[04/18/25]
Let's get some abstract ideas and a general framework down. I think a good idea would be to have a state machine for things like being in writing mode (i.e: does the text field have focus) or (if I implement it) Vim-esque modes like "command mode". I also think that isolating the text-rendering functionality right off the bat is a good idea, so I can implement a basic console printout in place of font rendering while I'm setting up/testing everything else (because lord knows that font rendering is gonna take the most time). All right, let's get started with a basic app, window, and console printout functionality (maybe even a text buffer?). Also, try to avoid using game-engine concepts where they aren't needed (mainly, don't just immediately make a main loop).